# The automated retry after a tool timeout in lit-legs.sh (plan 5.17.9, M24),
# checked as timeout-retry.test checks lit-legs.ps1's: after a lit run of a
# leg fails, the script runs 'lit-retry.py select' on the run's xunit file;
# when every failed test is timeout-only (a timeout marker after the last
# '# executed command:' line of its failure) and at most three are, each of
# them runs again, alone, with exactly the run's parameters and paths, -j1 and
# --filter=^<escaped name>$, into <build>/lit-results/<leg>-retry-<stem>.log
# and .xml, but only after a lit run that exited 1 (failed tests only) after
# running every test. The row passes with a detail that starts 'retried after
# timeout: <names> (<logs>)' when every re-run passes; it fails when a re-run
# fails, when more than three tests timed out, when a failure is not
# timeout-only, when lit reported an error or when lit did not run every test
# (and then nothing runs again). The stand-in llvm-lit of Inputs/ci-legs.py
# plays a scenario, inside WSL from Windows (the WSL legs) and natively on
# Linux. With --leg more-levels (msil/test/M1):
# (a) one timeout-only failure that passes when it runs again: PASS with the
# retry detail; the re-run passes the first run's parameters and path (the
# same lit arguments, matched by backreference) after -j1, its own xunit file
# and the filter; its log and xunit file exist.
# (b) the re-run times out again: FAIL, naming the re-run's log and status.
# (c) four timeout-only failures: FAIL with '4 tests timed out; re-run the leg
# on a quieter host', no re-run, and (b)'s retry files are gone. (d) a
# failure that is not timeout-only: FAIL, no re-run. (e) one of two re-runs
# fails: FAIL, with both re-runs named. (f) no xunit file: FAIL, no re-run.
# (g) three timeouts that pass again: PASS (three is the limit). (h) a timeout
# with a failure of another kind: FAIL, no re-run. (i) lit exits 2 after an
# error in tests (a test whose outcome is 'crash': lit's 'a worker process
# crashed' error, and the tests it did not run skipped in the xunit file) with
# one timeout-only failure: FAIL with 'lit reported an error, so no retry', no
# re-run and no retry file; the same xunit file with lit exit 1 (that test
# only skipped, as after --max-failures, which stops lit without an error)
# fails with 'lit did not run 2 test(s), so no retry', again without a re-run
# or a retry file; a lit error without a failed test still ends 'the xunit
# file lists no failed test, so no retry'. (j) With --leg net8, whose
# --filter-out excludes Programs/, an excluded and an unsupported test (each a
# <skipped> element with another message than 'Skipped') do not stop the
# retry: PASS as in (a).
# REQUIRES: msil-ci-bash

# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/ci-legs.py setup %t/build

# (a)
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/ci-legs.py scenario %t/build 'MSIL :: M1/a.c=timeout,pass' 'MSIL :: M1/b.c=pass'
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/ci-legs.py sh --distro %{legs_wsl_distro} %t/build MSIL_CI_RESULTS=%t/rows-a -- --leg more-levels > %t/a.log
# RUN: %{harness_check} contains %t/rows-a "^lit-legs\tmore-levels\tPASS\t\d+\tretried after timeout: MSIL :: M1/a\.c \(\S+/lit-results/more-levels-retry-MSIL_M1_a\.c\.log\); passed 1, failed 1; lit exit 1$"
# RUN: %{harness_check} contains %t/build/lit-calls.log '\Aarg: -sv\narg: --xunit-xml-output=\S+/lit-results/more-levels\.xml\n((?:arg: --param\narg: \S+\n)+)arg: (\S+/msil/test/M1)\narg: -sv\narg: -j1\narg: --xunit-xml-output=\S+/lit-results/more-levels-retry-MSIL_M1_a\.c\.xml\narg: --filter=\^MSIL :: M1/a\\\.c\$\n\1arg: \2\n\Z'
# RUN: %{harness_check} contains %t/build/lit-calls.log "^arg: msil_require_hosted=1$" "^arg: msil_glibc_sysroot=/$"
# RUN: %{harness_check} contains %t/build/lit-results/more-levels-retry-MSIL_M1_a.c.log "^PASS: MSIL :: M1/a\.c \(1 of 1\)$"
# RUN: %{harness_check} contains %t/build/lit-results/more-levels-retry-MSIL_M1_a.c.xml "<testcase classname=\"MSIL\.M1\" name=\"a\.c\" time=\"[0-9.]+\"/>"
# RUN: %{harness_check} contains %t/a.log "re-run after timeout of MSIL :: M1/a\.c: "

